0,Kajuk language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kajuk_language,"Language family. Niger–Congo?The Kajuk language, Ekajuk (also spelled Akajo and Akajuk), is an Ekoid language (of the Niger–Congo family) spoken in the Cross River State and some surrounding regions of Nigeria. The Ekajuk are one of several peoples who use the nsibidi ideographs.",Ekajuk,Niger-Congo
